# Lean context

Keep each turn cheap. Extra exploration is worse than asking one short question.

- Start from the user's paths, errors, and names. Do not scan the whole repo.
- Prefer `Grep` with a tight pattern and path. Avoid `**` globs and "read everything."
- Read only the needed slice (`offset`/`limit`). Default max ~80 lines unless the user asked for a full file.
- Cap first-pass tools at 4. Stop when you can act. No parallel "just in case" reads.
- Do not launch explore/subagents for a single file or a named symbol.
- Do not dump file contents, git status, or long logs into the reply.
- Do not re-read files already in this chat unless they may have changed.
- If the target is unclear after one targeted search, ask one specific question instead of widening the search.
